{"name":"El Niño","hex":"#d0cacd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"El Niño","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An invasion of warm water into the surface of the Pacific Ocean off the coast of Peru and Ecuador, the positive phase of the multi-year ENSO  cycle, which causes changes in local and regional climate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/El_Ni%C3%B1o"}],"entries":[{"title":"El Niño (Def Squad album)","blocks":[{"text":"El Niño is the only studio album by American hip-hop group Def Squad, composed of rappers Redman, Erick Sermon and Keith Murray. It was released on June 30, 1998, via Def Squad Records, Def Jam Recordings and Jive Records. The recording sessions took place at Mirror Image Recordings in Dix Hills, New York. The album was produced by Erick Sermon and Redman. It features guest appearances from Biz Markie, Mally G, Too $hort, and the Drama Squad."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/19/Def_Squad_-_El_Nino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Ni%C3%B1o_(Def_Squad_album)"},{"title":"El Niño (opera)","blocks":[{"text":"El Niño is an opera-oratorio by the contemporary American composer John Adams. It was premiered on December 15, 2000, at the Théâtre du Châtelet in Paris by soloists Dawn Upshaw, Lorraine Hunt Lieberson, and Willard White, the vocal ensemble Theatre of Voices, the London Voices, La Maîtrise de Paris, and the Deutsches Symphonie-Orchester Berlin, with Kent Nagano conducting. It has been performed on a number of occasions since, and has been broadcast on BBC Television."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/JA-portrait-1-LW.jpg/330px-JA-portrait-1-LW.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Ni%C3%B1o_(opera)"},{"title":"El Niño–Southern Oscillation","blocks":[{"text":"El Niño–Southern Oscillation (ENSO) is a global climate phenomenon that emerges from variation in winds and sea surface temperatures over the tropical Pacific Ocean. Those variations have an irregular pattern, but do have some appearance of cycles. The occurrence of ENSO is not easily predictable. It affects the climate of much of the tropics and subtropics, and has links (teleconnections) to higher-latitude regions of the world. The warming phase of the sea surface temperature is known as \"El Niño\" and the cooling phase as \"La Niña\". The Southern Oscillation is the accompanying atmospheric oscillation, which is coupled with the sea temperature change."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/NOAA_Nino.jpg/330px-NOAA_Nino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El_Ni%C3%B1o%E2%80%93Southern_Oscillation"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/NOAA_Nina.jpg/500px-NOAA_Nina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/NOAA_Nina.jpg/500px-NOAA_Nina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANOAA_Nina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/LaNina.png/500px-LaNina.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/LaNina.png/500px-LaNina.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The West Pacific is typically warmer than the East Pacific. The warmer water in the West Pacific leads to: more clouds, more rainfall, and a lower air pressure. The buildup of warm waters towards the west also leads to a thicker layer of warm ocean water that lowers the depth of the thermocline.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaNina.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fig4a_ENSOindices_Nino3.4only_large.png/500px-Fig4a_ENSOindices_Nino3.4only_large.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fig4a_ENSOindices_Nino3.4only_large.png/500px-Fig4a_ENSOindices_Nino3.4only_large.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFig4a_ENSOindices_Nino3.4only_large.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Sst_9798_animated.gif/330px-Sst_9798_animated.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Sst_9798_animated.gif/330px-Sst_9798_animated.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A loop of the 1997–98 El Niño event showing extreme sea surface temperature (SST) anomalies in the east tropical Pacific","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASst_9798_animated.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Sea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg/500px-Sea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Sea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg/1280px-Sea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Sea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg/500px-Sea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea surface temperature anomalies in November 2007, showing La Niña conditions","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea_Surface_Temperature_-_November_2007.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/NinoRegions.png/500px-NinoRegions.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/NinoRegions.png/500px-NinoRegions.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"Niño regions\" where sea surface temperatures are monitored to determine the current ENSO phase (warm or cold)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANinoRegions.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/El_Ni%C3%B1o_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png/500px-El_Ni%C3%B1o_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/El_Ni%C3%B1o_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png/500px-El_Ni%C3%B1o_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"El Niño influence on hurricane season activity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEl_Ni%C3%B1o_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/La_Ni%C3%B1a_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png/500px-La_Ni%C3%B1a_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/La_Ni%C3%B1a_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png/500px-La_Ni%C3%B1a_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"La Niña influence on hurricane season activity","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa_Ni%C3%B1a_influence_on_hurricane_season_activity.png"}],"sounds":{"El Niño":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b